# Application Handler Organization

## Folder layout

CQRS write/read handlers stay in vertical slices. Reactive/async handlers live under `handlers/`:

```
application/
├── commands/{use-case}/{use-case}.handler.ts   ← @CommandHandler
├── queries/{use-case}/{use-case}.handler.ts    ← @QueryHandler
└── handlers/
    ├── events/on-{event}/on-{event}.handler.ts ← @EventsHandler
    ├── workflow/{task}.handler.ts              ← @WorkflowTaskHandler
    └── queue/{job}.handler.ts                  ← @QueueHandler (+ {job}.job.ts)
```

## Rules

| Handler type | Location | Class name |
|---|---|---|
| Command | `commands/{use-case}/` | `{UseCase}Handler` |
| Query | `queries/{use-case}/` | `{UseCase}Handler` |
| Domain event | `handlers/events/on-{event}/` | `On{Event}Handler` |
| Workflow task | `handlers/workflow/` | `{Task}Handler` |
| Queue job | `handlers/queue/` | `{Job}Handler` |

## Do / Don't

```typescript
// ✅ Event handler — subfolder per event
application/handlers/events/on-user-deleted/on-user-deleted.handler.ts

// ✅ Queue — handler + job class co-located
application/handlers/queue/create-donation.handler.ts
application/handlers/queue/create-donation.job.ts

// ❌ Flat event files (no subfolder)
application/handlers/events/on-token-revoked.handler.ts

// ❌ Aggregated multi-handler files (split into vertical slices)
application/handlers/milestone.handlers.ts

// ❌ One top-level handlers/ folder for CQRS commands/queries
application/handlers/commands/create-user.handler.ts
```

## Cross-cutting integration (host app)

`apps/api/src/shared/integrations/{domain}/handlers/{events,workflow,queue}/` for glue that spans modules.

Domain workflow tasks stay in the owning module: `{module}/application/handlers/workflow/`.

## Package queue processors

Shared packages keep BullMQ processors in `infrastructure/queue/` (not `application/handlers/queue/`). Job **class definitions** stay in `application/jobs/`.

## Registration

Register all handler classes in the owning `*.module.ts` `providers` array — Nest does not auto-discover handlers.
